\section{Expected Benefits and Deliverables}

\subsection{Deliverables}

\begin{itemize}[nosep]
    \item Source code repository with \texttt{relulayer-core}, \texttt{relulayer-ffi}, and HIL harness.
    \item \texttt{relulayer\_hil.elf} verified for STM32H743 / Pixhawk 6X.
    \item Host/target equivalence regression suite with deterministic output traces.
    \item Phase I Final Report and non-proprietary technical summary.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Benefits to the Army}

ReluLayer reduces the risk of autonomous flight-control failures by adding a certifiable, low-latency safety boundary. It enables faster qualification of advanced guidance controllers while preserving deterministic fallback behavior. The technology is portable across ARM Cortex-M autopilots and can be adapted to rotorcraft, fixed-wing, and future VTOL platforms.

\section{Company Qualifications}

Atelier Logic Group LLC has direct experience in embedded flight software, formal methods, and Rust for safety-critical systems. The team has delivered DO-178C artifacts for multiple UAS platforms and maintains an active HIL regression environment for ARM Cortex-M7 targets. Prior work includes deterministic safety monitors, fixed-point control libraries, and host-target equivalence verification frameworks.

\section{Intellectual Property and Data Rights}

All technical data and computer software generated under this Phase I effort will be marked in accordance with DFARS 252.227-7018. Atelier Logic Group LLC has filed \textbf{Patent Pending} USPTO Provisional Patent Application VI (Serial No.~64/124,094, Confirmation No.~2105, Priority Date August~1, 2026, Attorney Docket \textbf{RELU-001-PPA6}), covering the deterministic bare-metal safety governor architecture, the Q16.16 fixed-point projection engine, the in-line physical data-bus co-processor with memory-mapped enforcement register and electronic inhibit line, and the zero-heap bare-metal integration method described in this technical volume. This application incorporates by reference in their entireties all prior provisional filings (PPA I--PPA V). The provisional filing does not affect the Government's rights under the SBIR data rights clause.

\paragraph{Dominant Abstract Data Disclaimer (Section 1.6 of PPA VI).} Notwithstanding the foregoing, all incoming flight workloads are treated purely as abstract multi-dimensional numerical state vectors, physical data bus signals, and polyhedral safety manifolds. Any higher-level commercial domain rules, schemas, or natural language descriptions are re-characterized as non-limiting background context to preserve robust subject-matter eligibility defenses under 35 U.S.C.~\S~101.

